DISCLAIMER

This package is an UNOFFICIAL community Linux port of the WorkBuddy
international-edition client (https://www.workbuddy.ai), which upstream does
not publish for Linux. It combines the official Windows application payload
with the Electron runtime and Linux helper binaries from Tencent's official
domestic-edition Linux package.

- WorkBuddy, WorkBuddy AI and CodeBuddy are products/trademarks of Tencent.
  This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Tencent.
- All application content is downloaded from Tencent's official servers at
  build time and is NOT redistributed by this package. The upstream software
  is proprietary; use of it is governed by Tencent's own Terms of Service and
  Privacy Policy.
- The Electron runtime, the bundled node/python session runtimes and the
  Linux CLI helpers come from Tencent's official domestic-edition
  (workbuddy.cn) Linux package. That Electron build carries the proprietary
  "workbuddyStorage" binding that sign-in depends on; stock Electron fails
  with CREDENTIAL_BOOTSTRAP_FAILED.
- Auto-update is non-functional on Linux (upstream publishes no Linux feed
  for the international edition). Upgrade by rebuilding this package.
- Known functional degradations versus the official macOS/Windows clients:
  Tencent Docs deep-collaboration engine (upstream publishes no Linux SDK for
  the current version; basic document read/write via cloud API still works),
  WeChat Pay plugin (no Linux build), and the enterprise IM channel backend
  (upstream's headless backend is used instead, as on the overseas build).
- Do NOT report issues with this port to Tencent's official support
  channels. File issues with the community port project instead.
